WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:12.610
89. What is beauty? Ideas of beauty are like the ocean. They change constantly, but

2
00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:18.170
they're always somehow the same. There are some things that have always been considered

3
00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:24.170
beautiful while other fashions come and go. Some beautiful qualities are the same across

4
00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:31.830
cultures and centuries. One important aspect of beauty is symmetry. Symmetry is balance.

5
00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:37.950
It refers to how alike two halves of an object are. Faces that are symmetrical are considered

6
00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:44.710
more beautiful than those that aren't. Signs of good health are also always called beautiful,

7
00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:50.310
such as shiny hair, clear skin, and strong teeth. Strong teeth don't necessarily have

8
00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:56.850
to be white, though. In some parts of Vietnam, black teeth are considered attractive. Other

9
00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:03.410
aspects of beauty change with time and geography. For example, our current obsession with thinness

10
00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:10.250
in much of the world is very new. Until recently, forty or fifty years ago, it was beautiful

11
00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:17.250
to be soft and round. Having some fat was considered beautiful throughout most of history.

12
00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:22.650
It meant that you were healthy and didn't have to work hard. Now we know that being

13
00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:30.290
fit is healthy, too. Being fit is something that takes time and effort and probably money.

14
00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:36.350
Being thin now shows status the way being fat did. Different cultures have different

15
00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:43.290
ideas of beauty. Some cultures in Africa and Asia value long necks. Women have their necks

16
00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:51.290
stretched with metal rings to achieve a beautiful look. In ancient China, bound feet were beautiful,

17
00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:57.210
though they prevented women from walking comfortably. In Renaissance Europe, high foreheads

18
00:01:57.210 --> 00:02:03.850
were regarded as beautiful, so women plucked their hair lines. Some ideas of beauty change

19
00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:10.090
with our opinions of health and status, but others stay the same. There are few rules

20
00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:16.730
about beauty. In the end, the most beautiful person in the world is the one you look at

21
00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:17.610
with love.
